ALVA — Implement the “Why Alva?” Dialogue

Objective

Implement the “Why Alva?” feature on the Home Screen of Alva.

When the player clicks or activates the existing “Why Alva?” text beneath the developer attribution, open a beautifully presented, readable dialogue explaining the personal story behind Alva, what inspired its creation, and what the project hopes to accomplish.

This must feel like a natural part of Alva’s existing interface, not an unrelated popup or a separate page.

The dialogue should be personal, sincere, easy to read, and welcoming.

Important: The story must never name, list, feature, suggest, or reference any specific fictional characters, regardless of whether they are currently playable, planned, or absent from the game. It must also never discuss the game’s roster or character availability.

1. Repository and Architecture

Repository: hiyroscript/alva

Before implementing, carefully examine the existing application structure and follow its conventions.

Relevant files:

* js/screens/home-screen.js — Home Screen and existing “Why Alva?” button.
* js/ui/overlays.js — Existing InfoDialog and ModalDialog implementations.
* js/core/app.js — Global dialogue instances and application state.
* css/home.css — Home Screen styling.
* css/overlays.css — Dialogue styling.
* css/responsive.css — Responsive layout.
* js/localization/strings/en.js — English localization.
* js/localization/strings/fr.js — French localization.
* js/localization/i18n.js — Translation system.
* ALVA_SPEC.md — Authoritative product specification.

Alva uses vanilla JavaScript ES modules, HTML, CSS, and Canvas 2D. Do not introduce additional frameworks, libraries, dependencies, or build systems.

The Home Screen already contains an enabled .home-why-alva button. Preserve this existing button, its label, its location, and its established appearance.

Replace its placeholder behavior with a working interaction.

2. Required Interaction

When the player activates “Why Alva?”:

1. A modal dialogue opens over the Home Screen.
2. The background is dimmed using Alva’s existing overlay styling.
3. The dialogue displays the heading “Why Alva?”
4. Beneath the heading, the creator’s story appears in properly separated paragraphs.
5. The player can scroll through the story if it exceeds the available vertical space.
6. A visible close button allows the player to dismiss the dialogue.
7. Closing returns the player to the Home Screen without changing navigation state or interrupting existing Home Screen functionality.

The dialogue must work with mouse, touch, keyboard, and supported controllers.

Support closing through the existing application’s navigation conventions, including Escape, controller Back, the close button, and clicking the backdrop.

Opening the dialogue repeatedly must work reliably.

3. Exact English Dialogue Content

Title: Why Alva?

I’ve always been a big fan of fiction, especially when it comes to superheroes. For a long time, I imagined a fighting game where characters from completely different worlds could face each other. Some games came close to making that idea a reality, but not all of them were successful, and others were exclusive to platforms I couldn’t access.

One day, while watching videos online, I discovered something called MUGEN. It’s a fighting game engine that allows people to create their own fighters using sprites and animations. I immediately fell in love with the idea. The creative freedom it offered was exactly what I had always wanted to experience. Unfortunately, I never owned a device that could run it.

That got me thinking. It’s unfortunate that people can miss out on something they would love simply because they don’t have the right device, or because downloading and setting up a game isn’t an option for them. I wanted to find a way to make that kind of experience easier for more people to enjoy.

And that’s how Alva began.

Inspired by the creative freedom behind MUGEN, I decided to create my own platform fighting game with a similar spirit, but with accessibility in mind. With Alva, there’s no need to download or install the game. All you have to do is open a link in your browser on a supported device and start playing.

Alva is an unofficial fan-made project, created out of a genuine love for fiction and the endless possibilities of bringing different worlds together. It’s a game made for people who share that same imagination and excitement.

And that’s why Alva exists.

Writing Requirements

Preserve the exact meaning and personal perspective of the story.

The dialogue should read like the creator is speaking directly to the player, not like corporate marketing or advertising copy.

Maintain the first-person perspective throughout.

Do not add:

* Specific fictional character names.
* Franchise names, other than MUGEN, which is essential to the creator’s story.
* References to playable, upcoming, unavailable, or desired characters.
* Promises about future features or unsupported devices.
* Claims that Alva is officially associated with MUGEN or any other property.
* Unnecessary promotional language.

The text should express the inspiration behind the project, without implying that Alva is built using the MUGEN engine.

